<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 715 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 715 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of September 26 raised 715 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 736 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 226 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.61 (14.61)	    82.0   (87.4)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.92 (16.92)	    92.0  (135.9)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.80 (17.80)	    99.0   (85.3)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.66 (21.68)	   442.0  (427.4)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,558.5 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,559 a week earlier.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056 645456</p>
